🚫 LIMITATIONS & SAFEGUARDS
No Automatic Message Reading (Message Content Intent!)
Bots cannot read message content in guilds (servers) unless explicitly granted the Message Content Intent (requires verification for larger bots).

This is to protect user privacy and avoid abuse.
Discord

Permission Hierarchy Constraints
A bot can only act on users/roles lower in the permission hierarchy than its highest role — cannot modify or manage peers or superiors.
Discord
Discord

Rate Limits & API Quotas
All actions—messages sent, invites created, bans issued—are subject to global and route-based rate limits.

Repeated spamming, flood calls, or abusing API endpoints triggers temporary bans or failures.
Discord

No Editing of Others’ Messages
Bots cannot edit messages authored by other users. The API does not support it, even for admin-level bots.

Modification workflows typically use deletion + a warning message.
